                                                                   328 1451
               PRELIMINARY EVALUATION FOR ENDF/B-VI                328 1451
                                                                   328 1451
 BASED ON AN UPDATE OF THE VARIANCE-COVARIANCE ANALYSIS PERFORMED  328 1451
 FOR ENDF/B-V.2 (YO81). INCLUDES NEW (N,NT) DATA THROUGH 1/1/88    328 1451
 (LI83, MA83, SM84, MA86, TA84, GO85, CH85, SW85, QA86), AS WELL   328 1451
 AS NEW ELASTIC AND INELASTIC DATA (CH85, SH84, AL82, DR86,        328 1451
 SC87, DE87).  SIMILAR TECHNIQUES TO YO82 WERE USED EXCEPT         328 1451
 CROSS CORRELATIONS AMONG (N,NT) MEASUREMENTS WERE INCLUDED.       328 1451
 IN ADDITION, A SEPARATE COVARIANCE ANALYSIS WAS PERFORMED FOR     328 1451
 THE (N,N2) DISCRETE INELASTIC CROSS SECTION TO THE 4.63-MEV       328 1451
 STATE OF LI7.  PRIMARY REFERENCE IS YO88.                         328 1451
 THE THERMAL NEUTRON DATA WERE UPDATED USING THE MU81 COMPILATION. 328 1451
                                                                   328 1451
 *********** GENERAL DESCRIPTION ********************************* 328 1451
                                                                   328 1451
   INDEPENDENT V-C ANALYSIS FOR THE FOLLOWING FOUR REACTIONS       328 1451
 WAS PERFORMED USING THE GLUCS CODE SYSTEM (HE80).                 328 1451
     (1) TOTAL X/S (MT1)                                           328 1451
     (2) ELASTIC + (N,NPRIME) X/S TO 1ST LEVEL (MT2+MT51)          328 1451
     (3) (N,NT) X/S (SUM OF MT52 THRU MT82)                        328 1451
     (4) (N,2N)+(N,2ND)+(N,3NP)+(N,D)  (MT16+MT24+MT25+MT104)      328 1451
 VARIANCES AND COVARIANCES FROM THE GLUCS ANALYSIS WERE THEN AD-   328 1451
 JUSTED WITH THE ALVIN CODE (HA75) UNDER THE CONSTRAINT THAT       328 1451
 REACTIONS (2)-(4) SUM TO REACTION (1). MOST CROSS SECTIONS        328 1451
 AND COVARIANCES IN MF=3 AND 33 ARE BASED ON THESE RESULTS.        328 1451
   A SEPARATE GLUCS ANALYSIS WAS PERFORMED OF MT51 X/S DATA AND    328 1451
 THEN SUBTRACTED FROM REACTION (2) TO OBTAIN MT2. TO SEPARATE      328 1451
 COMPONENT MTS FROM REACTION (4), MT104 FROM ENDF/B-V.1 WAS        328 1451
 ADOPTED, AND AD HOC CURVES WERE DRAWN FOR MT16+MT24 AND MT25      328 1451
 USING THE MEAGER EXP DATA. MT16 AND MT24 WERE THEN SEPARATED      328 1451
 USING STATISTICAL THEORY CALCULATIONS.                            328 1451
   COVARIANCE MATRICES WERE DEVELOPED FOR EACH EXPERIMENT. IN      328 1451
 MOST CASES STANDARD DEVIATIONS WERE AVAILABLE BUT IT WAS USUALLY  328 1451
 NECESSARY TO MAKE GENERIC ASSUMPTIONS FOR THE ERROR CORRELATIONS  328 1451
 ACCORDING TO THE TYPE OF MEASUREMENT. EXPERIMENTAL DATA INCLUDED  328 1451
 IN THE ANALYSIS ARE REFERENCED BELOW.  CROSS CORRELATIONS         328 1451
 BETWEEN DIFFERENT TRITIUM-PROD.EXPERIMENTS DUE TO STANDARDS       328 1451
 AND TRITIUM HALF LIFE WERE INCLUDED IN V-C ANALYSIS.              328 1451
                                                                   328 1451
 *********** MF=2 RESONANCE PARAMETERS *************************** 328 1451
                                                                   328 1451
 MT=151  SCATTERING RADIUS ONLY.                                   328 1451
                                                                   328 1451
 *********** MF=3 SMOOTH NEUTRON CROSS SECTIONS ****************** 328 1451
                                                                   328 1451
 MT=  1  TOTAL CROSS SECTION. ENDF/B-V.1 ADOPTED BELOW 0.1 MEV     328 1451
         EXCEPT THE THERMAL DATA OF MU81 WAS USED AND THE ELAST.   328 1451
         DATA OF AL82 WAS MATCHED.  V-C ANALYSIS ABOVE 0.1         328 1451
         MEV BASED ON ME70, GO71, HA78, FO71, KA57, BR58, PE60,    328 1451
         CO52, LA79, AND HI68. ERRORS DOUBLED NEAR 260-KEV         328 1451
         RESONANCE FOR HI68, ME70 DATA.                            328 1451
 MT=  2  ELASTIC CROSS SECTION. V-C ANALYSIS USED DATA OF TH56,    328 1451
         WI56, KN68, BA63A, HO68, LI80, CO67, WO62, RE66, AR64,    328 1451
         HY68, LA61, KN81, KN79, HO79, LA64, CH85, SH84, AND       328 1451
         DR86.  THE ERRORS IN THE V-C ANALYSIS WERE TRIPLED NEAR   328 1451
         260-KEV RESONANCE FOR LA61, LA64 DATA. OPTICAL MODEL      328 1451
         ANALYSIS OF HO79 DATA USED TO CALCULATE X/S ABOVE         328 1451
         14 MEV FOR V-C ANALYSIS. THERMAL CROSS SECTION OF MU81    328 1451
         USED, AND EVALUATION MATCHED TO AL82 DATA BELOW 0.1 MEV.  328 1451
 MT=  4  (N,NPRIME)GAMMA + (N,NPRIME)ALPHA-T.  SUM OF MT=51-82.    328 1451
 MT= 16  (N,2N) CROSS SECTION.  V-C ANALYSIS OF MT16+MT24 USED     328 1451
         DATA OF CH85, AS58, MC61, MA69. SEPARATION OF MT16 AND    328 1451
         MT24 FOLLOWS THE RATIO OF THE ENDF/B-V.1 DATA.            328 1451
 MT= 24  (N,2N)ALPHA-D CROSS SECTION.  SEE COMMENT FOR MT16.       328 1451
 MT= 25  (N,3N)ALPHA-P CROSS SECTION.  SMOOTH CURVE DRAWN ABOVE 14 328 1451
         MEV SO AS TO APPROXIMATELY AGREE WITH MA69, KO71 DATA.    328 1451
 MT= 51  (N,NPRIME)GAMMA CROSS SECTION.  SEPARATE V-C ANALYSIS     328 1451
         USED DATA OF PR72, OL80, SM76, DI74, MO78, FR55, KN81,    328 1451
         BE60, BA53, CH61, KN68, GL63, HO68, BA63A. ERRORS         328 1451
         DOUBLED ON FR55, BE60, AND TRIPLED ON CH61.               328 1451
 MT= 56  (N,NPRIME)ALPHA-T CROSS SECTION.  SEPARATE V-C ANALYSIS   328 1451
         PERFORMED USING DATA OF CH85, DR87, SC87, DE87, RE66,     328 1451
         AR64, HY68, WO62, CO67, BI77, HO79, BA79, BA63, LI80,     328 1451
         HO68, RO62 AND YO65.                                      328 1451
 MT=52-82 (N,NPRIME)ALPHA-T CROSS SECTION.  EXCEPT FOR MT56,       328 1451
         EXCITATION ENERGY BINS WERE CONSTRUCTED SUCH THAT CALCU-  328 1451
         LATED NEUTRON EMISSION SPECTRA AGREE WITH THE MEASURE-    328 1451
         MENTS BY LI80 AT 5.96, 9.83, AND 14.1 MEV INCIDENT ENER-  328 1451
         GY. INTERPOLATION OF CROSS SECTIONS BETWEEN ENERGIES      328 1451
         BASED ON LINEAR INTERPOLATION OF COMPUTED CM EMISSION     328 1451
         SPECTRA, SUITABLY CONTRACTED OR EXPANDED TO CONSERVE      328 1451
         ENERGY.  ABOVE 14.1 MEV, THE EXP EMISSION SHAPE WAS USED  328 1451
         TO INFER THE X/S, WITH THE SHAPES AGAIN SUITABLY EX-      328 1451
         PANDED TO CONSERVE ENERGY.                                328 1451
         AT ALL INCIDENT ENERGIES, THE SUM OF MT=52-82 WAS         328 1451
         CONSTRAINED TO EQUAL THE (N,NT) CROSS SECTION FROM THE    328 1451
         VARIANCE-COVARIANCE ANALYSIS.                             328 1451
 MT=102  (N,GAMMA) CROSS SECTION.  SHAPE FROM ENDF/B-V.1 EXCEPT    328 1451
         DATA RAISED ABOVE 10 EV TO AGREE WITH EXP.DATA (IM59).    328 1451
         THERMAL CROSS SECTION OF MU81 USED.                       328 1451
 MT=104  (N,D) CROSS SECTION.  ADOPTED FROM ENDF/B-V.1. DATA       328 1451
         AGREE APPROXIMATELY WITH EXPS OF BA53, BA63B, LI73,       328 1451
         AND DISAGREE WITH MI61.                                   328 1451
